<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="<%= locals.uiTheme || 'dark' %>" data-density="<%= locals.uiDensity || 'comfortable' %>" data-style="<%= locals.uiStyle || 'cards' %>">
<head>
<%- include('partials/site-head', { title: 'D&D 5e guide · CertiFried', description: 'How to play the Dungeons & Dragons 5e game in Discord with the CertiFried bot and its AI Dungeon Master: characters, sessions, rolls, rests, combat, dungeons, parties and PvP.', path: '/docs/rpg' }) %>
    <style>
        .rpg-crumb { margin: 0 0 var(--cf-3); font-size: var(--cf-text-sm); color: var(--cf-text-3); }
        .rpg-crumb a { color: var(--cf-text-2); text-decoration: none; }
        .rpg-crumb a:hover { color: var(--cf-text); text-decoration: underline; }
        .rpg-code { display: block; margin: 0 0 var(--cf-4); padding: 10px 14px; overflow-x: auto; font-family: var(--cf-mono); font-size: var(--cf-text-sm); color: var(--cf-text); background: var(--cf-inset); border: 1px solid var(--cf-border); border-radius: var(--cf-radius); white-space: pre; }
        .rpg-cols { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--cf-3); margin: 0 0 var(--cf-4); }
        @media (max-width: 640px) { .rpg-cols { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } }
        .rpg-cols > div { padding: var(--cf-3) var(--cf-4); background: var(--cf-surface); border: 1px solid var(--cf-border); border-radius: var(--cf-radius-lg); }
        .rpg-cols h3 { margin: 0 0 4px; font-size: var(--cf-text-md); }
        .rpg-cols p { margin: 0; font-size: var(--cf-text-sm); }
    </style>
</head>
<body class="cfs-body">
<%- include('partials/site-header', { active: 'docs', user: locals.user || null, returnTo: '/docs/rpg' }) %>
    <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1" class="cfs-main cfs-main--wide">
        <div class="cfs-pagehead">
            <p class="rpg-crumb"><a href="/docs">Documentation</a> / D&amp;D guide</p>
            <h1>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5e guide</h1>
            <p class="cfs-lede">How to play the D&amp;D 5e game in Discord. An AI Dungeon Master runs the story; the bot keeps your character sheet, rolls the dice and follows the 5e rules.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="cfs-doc">
            <nav class="cfs-toc" aria-label="On this page">
                <h2>Getting started</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li><a href="#quickstart">Quick start</a></li>
                    <li><a href="#character">Character creation</a></li>
                    <li><a href="#statrolling">Ability scores</a></li>
                </ul>
                <h2>Playing</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li><a href="#aidm">The AI Dungeon Master</a></li>
                    <li><a href="#mechanics">Death saves, exhaustion, inspiration</a></li>
                    <li><a href="#rest">Resting</a></li>
                    <li><a href="#more">Combat, dungeons, parties, PvP</a></li>
                </ul>
                <h2>Reference</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li><a href="#inventory">Inventory</a></li>
                    <li><a href="#continuity">Story and progress</a></li>
                    <li><a href="#commands">Commands</a></li>
                    <li><a href="#tips">Tips</a></li>
                </ul>
            </nav>

            <div class="cfs-prose">
                <h2 id="quickstart">Quick start</h2>
                <p>The <code>/rpg</code> commands are not in Discord's <code>/</code> menu. Type them as a normal message, starting with <code>/rpg</code>, and give options as <code>name:value</code>, as in the examples on this page.</p>
                <h3>1. Create a character</h3>
                <code class="rpg-code">/rpg character create name:Thorin class:Fighter species:Dwarf background:Soldier</code>
                <h3>2. Start an adventure</h3>
                <code class="rpg-code">/rpg session start</code>
                <h3>3. Say what you do</h3>
                <p>Reply to the Dungeon Master's message, or type in the server's RPG channel if an admin has set one with <code>/rpg settings channel</code>. <code>/rpg play action</code> works anywhere.</p>
                <div class="cfs-note">
                    <p>"I search the room for hidden doors"<br>"I attack the goblin with my sword"<br>"I try to persuade the guard to let us pass"</p>
                </div>

                <h2 id="character">Character creation</h2>
                <h3>Classes (12)</h3>
                <p>Barbarian, Bard, Cleric, Druid, Fighter, Monk, Paladin, Ranger, Rogue, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard.</p>
                <h3>Species (31, counting subraces)</h3>
                <p>Human (and variant human), elf (high, wood, dark), dwarf (hill, mountain), halfling (lightfoot, stout), dragonborn, gnome (rock, forest), half-elf, half-orc, tiefling, aasimar, goliath, tabaxi, kenku, tortle, aarakocra, genasi, firbolg, yuan-ti, changeling, warforged, and custom. A species the bot does not know is treated as human.</p>
                <h3>Backgrounds (15)</h3>
                <p>Acolyte, Charlatan, Criminal, Entertainer, Far Traveler, Folk Hero, Guild Artisan, Haunted One, Hermit, Noble, Outlander, Sage, Sailor, Soldier, Urchin. Each background gives two skill proficiencies; Haunted One gives Investigation and Survival. The name can be typed with spaces, underscores or hyphens (<code>far traveler</code> or <code>far_traveler</code>).</p>
                <h3>Species bonuses</h3>
                <p>Applied automatically when the character is created. Some examples:</p>
                <div class="cfs-table-wrap">
                    <table>
                        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Species</th><th scope="col">Bonus</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td>Dwarf</td><td>+2 CON; darkvision, dwarven resilience, stonecunning</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Elf</td><td>+2 DEX; darkvision, fey ancestry, trance</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Human</td><td>+1 to every ability score; an extra language</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Tiefling</td><td>+2 CHA, +1 INT; darkvision, hellish resistance, infernal legacy</td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
                <p>You can also import a filled-in character sheet: send <code>/rpg character import</code> with the PDF attached to the message.</p>

                <h2 id="statrolling">Ability scores</h2>
                <p>Three ways to set them:</p>
                <div class="rpg-cols">
                    <div><h3>Roll</h3><p><code>/rpg statroll roll</code> rolls 4d6 six times and drops the lowest die each time. For example 6, 5, 4, 2 gives 15.</p></div>
                    <div><h3>Standard array</h3><p><code>/rpg statroll standard</code> uses 15, 14, 13, 12, 10, 8.</p></div>
                    <div><h3>Point buy</h3><p><code>/rpg statroll pointbuy</code>: every score starts at 8 and you spend 27 points.</p></div>
                </div>

                <h2 id="aidm">The AI Dungeon Master</h2>
                <p><code>/rpg session start</code> begins a scene built around your character's class, species, level and backstory. The Dungeon Master is Google Gemini, prompted with the 5e rules and your campaign's history.</p>
                <p>Write what your character does in plain words: actions ("I kick down the door"), dialogue ("I ask the merchant about the missing shipment"), combat ("I cast fireball at the enemies") or exploration ("I examine the strange runes"). The Dungeon Master then:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>decides what happens and asks for a roll when one is needed (roll buttons appear on the message),</li>
                    <li>applies damage, healing and conditions,</li>
                    <li>keeps track of the story: people you meet remember you and places stay as you left them,</li>
                    <li>uses 5e difficulty classes, saving throws and combat rules.</li>
                </ul>
                <h3>Difficulty classes</h3>
                <div class="cfs-table-wrap">
                    <table>
                        <thead><tr><th scope="col">DC</th><th scope="col">Difficulty</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td>5</td><td>Very easy</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>10</td><td>Easy</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>15</td><td>Medium</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>20</td><td>Hard</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>25</td><td>Very hard</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>30</td><td>Nearly impossible</td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>

                <h2 id="mechanics">Death saves, exhaustion and inspiration</h2>
                <h3>Death saving throws</h3>
                <p><code>/rpg condition deathsave</code>. 10 or higher is a success, below 10 a failure. A natural 1 counts as two failures; a natural 20 brings you back with 1 HP. Three successes and you are stable; three failures and the character dies.</p>
                <h3>Exhaustion</h3>
                <p><code>/rpg condition exhaustion</code> shows your level. The Dungeon Master adds and removes levels.</p>
                <div class="cfs-table-wrap">
                    <table>
                        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Level</th><th scope="col">Effect</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td>1</td><td>Disadvantage on ability checks</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>2</td><td>Speed halved</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>3</td><td>Disadvantage on attacks and saving throws</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>4</td><td>Hit point maximum halved</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>5</td><td>Speed reduced to 0</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>6</td><td>Death</td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
                <h3>Inspiration</h3>
                <p><code>/rpg condition inspiration</code>. The Dungeon Master grants it for good roleplay; spend it for advantage on a roll.</p>

                <h2 id="rest">Resting</h2>
                <h3>Short rest (1 hour)</h3>
                <code class="rpg-code">/rpg rest short hit_dice:2</code>
                <p>Spend hit dice to heal: each die heals its roll plus your CON modifier.</p>
                <h3>Long rest (8 hours)</h3>
                <code class="rpg-code">/rpg rest long</code>
                <ul>
                    <li>All hit points back</li>
                    <li>All spell slots back</li>
                    <li>Half your hit dice back</li>
                    <li>One level of exhaustion removed</li>
                </ul>

                <h2 id="more">Combat, dungeons, parties and PvP</h2>
                <p>Outside a story session there is more to do:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Combat</strong>: <code>/rpg combat enemies</code> lists foes to fight and <code>/rpg combat fight</code> starts a turn-based fight.</li>
                    <li><strong>Quests</strong>: <code>/rpg quest list</code>, <code>/rpg quest start</code>, <code>/rpg quest complete</code>.</li>
                    <li><strong>Dungeons</strong>: <code>/rpg dungeon enter</code> on Easy, Normal, Hard or Nightmare, then <code>/rpg dungeon advance</code> room by room.</li>
                    <li><strong>Shop</strong>: <code>/rpg shop browse</code>, <code>buy</code> and <code>sell</code>.</li>
                    <li><strong>Parties</strong>: <code>/rpg party create</code> and <code>/rpg party invite</code> to play together.</li>
                    <li><strong>PvP</strong>: <code>/rpg pvp challenge</code> for a duel, a ranked match or a tournament, with a leaderboard (<code>/rpg pvp leaderboard</code>).</li>
                    <li><strong>Spells</strong>: <code>/rpg spell cast</code>, <code>/rpg spell slots</code>, <code>/rpg spell learn</code>.</li>
                    <li><strong>Campaigns</strong>: <code>/rpg campaign create</code> for a homebrew, official-module or hybrid campaign that others join with <code>/rpg campaign join</code>.</li>
                </ul>

                <h2 id="inventory">Inventory</h2>
                <code class="rpg-code">/rpg inventory view
/rpg inventory equip item_id:5
/rpg inventory unequip item_id:5</code>
                <p>Items come from defeated enemies, the shop, quest rewards and exploring.</p>

                <h2 id="continuity">Story and progress</h2>
                <p>Your adventure carries over between sessions. The bot saves:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>your recent actions and the Dungeon Master's replies,</li>
                    <li>where you are and what the scene looks like,</li>
                    <li>the people you have met and how they feel about you,</li>
                    <li>quests (active, completed, failed) and events in the world.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>The Dungeon Master is given this history each time, so the story stays consistent. <code>/rpg journal map</code>, <code>/rpg journal quests</code> and <code>/rpg journal npcs</code> show your map, your quests and the people you have met.</p>
                <h3>Experience and levels</h3>
                <p>You earn XP from combat, quests and roleplay, and level up as soon as you have enough. Each level raises your hit points and proficiency bonus and unlocks class features. <code>/rpg stats leaderboard</code> ranks players in the server.</p>

                <h2 id="commands">Commands</h2>
                <div class="cfs-table-wrap">
                    <table class="cfs-table-stack">
                        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Command</th><th scope="col">What it does</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td><code>/rpg character create</code></td><td data-label="Does">Make a character</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>/rpg character view</code></td><td data-label="Does">Character sheet</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>/rpg character stats</code></td><td data-label="Does">Detailed statistics</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>/rpg character delete</code></td><td data-label="Does">Delete your character</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>/rpg session start</code></td><td data-label="Does">Start a story with the Dungeon Master</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>/rpg session end</code></td><td data-label="Does">End the session with a recap</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>/rpg play action</code></td><td data-label="Does">Say what your character does</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>/rpg roll dice</code></td><td data-label="Does">Roll any dice, e.g. 2d6+3</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>/rpg inventory view</code></td><td data-label="Does">Your items</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>/rpg rest short</code> / <code>long</code></td><td data-label="Does">Rest to recover</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>/rpg condition deathsave</code></td><td data-label="Does">Make a death saving throw</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>/rpg statroll roll</code></td><td data-label="Does">Roll ability scores (4d6, drop the lowest)</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>/rpg guide overview</code></td><td data-label="Does">This guide inside Discord</td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
                <p>Every <code>/rpg</code> command and its options are in the <a href="/commands#rpg">command list</a>.</p>

                <h2 id="tips">Tips</h2>
                <ol>
                    <li><strong>Be specific.</strong> "I carefully search under the bed" works better than "search".</li>
                    <li><strong>Stay in character.</strong> The Dungeon Master writes a better story when you roleplay.</li>
                    <li><strong>Use the scene.</strong> Refer to things the Dungeon Master has described.</li>
                    <li><strong>Ask.</strong> "Do I notice anything unusual?" leads to a Perception check.</li>
                    <li><strong>Play together.</strong> In a party, agree on a plan before you act.</li>
                </ol>
            </div>
        </div>
    </main>
<%- include('partials/site-footer') %>
<script>
(function () {
    var links = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('.cfs-toc a[href^="#"]'));
    if (!('IntersectionObserver' in window) || !links.length) return;
    var byId = {};
    links.forEach(function (a) { byId[a.getAttribute('href').slice(1)] = a; });
    var obs = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
        entries.forEach(function (e) {
            if (!e.isIntersecting) return;
            links.forEach(function (a) { a.classList.remove('is-current'); });
            if (byId[e.target.id]) byId[e.target.id].classList.add('is-current');
        });
    }, { rootMargin: '-64px 0px -70% 0px' });
    Object.keys(byId).forEach(function (id) { var el = document.getElementById(id); if (el) obs.observe(el); });
})();
</script>
</body>
</html>
